VeridianOS: qtbase: no moc run for qttemporalpattern_p.h outside developer builds

time/qttemporalpattern_p.h declares its namespace for moc
(Q_NAMESPACE_EXPORT, Q_FLAG_NS) only under QT_BUILD_INTERNAL, which Qt
defines for developer builds (configure.cmake: qt_feature_definition
"developer-build" "QT_BUILD_INTERNAL"). AutoMoc does not evaluate #ifdef,
saw the macro and ran moc, which in any other build found nothing:
"qttemporalpattern_p.h: note: No relevant classes found. No output
generated." (host and target Qt). The header is now excluded from AutoMoc
unless developer_build is on; developer builds are unchanged, and the
other builds lose an empty moc run.

--- a/src/corelib/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/corelib/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1124,6 +1124,12 @@
         parse/qtparseqttemporalformat.cpp parse/qtparseqttemporalformat_p.h
 )
 
+# The header declares its namespace for moc only in developer builds
+# (QT_BUILD_INTERNAL); elsewhere moc would have nothing to generate.
+if(NOT QT_FEATURE_developer_build)
+    set_source_files_properties(time/qttemporalpattern_p.h PROPERTIES SKIP_AUTOMOC ON)
+endif()
+
 qt_internal_extend_target(Core CONDITION QT_FEATURE_datetimeparser
     SOURCES
         time/qdatetimeparser.cpp time/qdatetimeparser_p.h
